        <strong>Quick answer:</strong> The Hebei wire mesh cluster — centered on Anping County, 250 km south of Beijing — is the densest wire mesh manufacturing region on earth, with an estimated 20,000+ factories and workshops producing the majority of China's wire mesh exports. That density cuts your costs by 30–50% versus domestic distributors, but the same hyper-competition (内卷, "involution") that drives prices down also pushes some factories to shave wire diameter, thin zinc coatings, and substitute steel grades. The winning strategy: quote the identical specification to 3–5 factories, normalize every quote to price per kilogram using a <a href="/tools/fob-price-calculator/" class="text-theme-primary underline">FOB price calculator</a>, order paid samples from the top two, and never accept a quote that is dramatically below the cluster average. This guide shows you how the cluster works, who makes what where, and how to use its competition to your advantage instead of becoming its victim.
      </p>
