      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-theme-primary mb-4">Why Anping: The Geography of the Cluster</h2>

      <p class="text-theme-secondary mb-4 leading-relaxed">
        Anping County sits on the North China Plain, roughly 250 km south of Beijing and 200 km southwest of Tianjin's Xingang port — the port through which most of the cluster's exports flow. The industry traces back to the 1880s; the township-enterprise boom of the 1980s turned it into a full production cluster. Today the county hosts hundreds of registered manufacturers plus thousands of workshops, ringed by wire drawing, galvanizing, PVC coating, and weaving-equipment suppliers in neighboring Hengshui, Shijiazhuang, and Cangzhou.
      </p>

      <p class="text-theme-secondary mb-4 leading-relaxed">
        This supply-chain density is the cluster's real moat. A gabion factory does not need to own a wire drawing line — a galvanizer twenty minutes away supplies GALFAN wire on demand. Raw steel arrives from Hebei's own mills (Tangshan, Handan), keeping input costs and lead times low. The result: RFQ to loaded container in three weeks.
      </p>

      <p class="text-theme-secondary mb-4 leading-relaxed">
        The commercial heart of the cluster is the county seat, home to the China Anping International Wire Mesh World trading market — a permanent showroom where hundreds of trading companies display samples of virtually every mesh made in the region. Read our dedicated <a href="/anping-wire-mesh/" class="text-theme-accent hover:underline">Anping wire mesh guide</a> for the county's industry structure and quality tiers.
      </p>

      <div class="bg-theme-secondary bg-opacity-10 border border-theme rounded-lg p-6">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-theme-primary mb-2">Why Geography Matters to You</h3>
        <p class="text-theme-secondary text-sm">
          Two practical consequences: (1) FOB Xingang/Tianjin quotes carry low inland freight, so cluster quotes are directly comparable — small price differences reflect real cost, not logistics. (2) Because subcontractors are minutes apart, factories quote custom configurations faster and cheaper than anywhere else.
        </p>
