    <!-- Involution -->
    <section id="involution" class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-theme-primary mb-4">How 内卷 (Involution) Shapes Prices and Service</h2>

      <p class="text-theme-secondary mb-4 leading-relaxed">
        Ask anyone in the Anping trade about the last five years and you will hear one word: 内卷 (nèijuǎn, "involution") — competition so intense that margins compress toward zero and factories fight for orders they barely profit from. The drivers are structural: national steel capacity far exceeds domestic demand, weaving machines are cheap and standardized, and export licenses keep multiplying.
      </p>

      <p class="text-theme-secondary mb-4 leading-relaxed">
        For overseas buyers, involution is a double-edged sword with very predictable effects on both sides:
      </p>

      <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-6">
        <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
