              <td class="p-3">Standard mesh often available from a single roll or pallet</td>
              <td class="p-3">Small orders get the factory's least attention at production time</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-theme">
              <td class="p-3 font-medium">Service arms race</td>
              <td class="p-3">Free loading plans, packing photos, inspection welcome, flexible payment</td>
              <td class="p-3">Service quality is a sales function — it evaporates after the deposit unless contractually anchored</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 font-medium">Specification creep</td>
              <td class="p-3">Some factories genuinely upgrade fittings, packaging, coatings to win orders</td>
              <td class="p-3">Others downgrade wire diameter or zinc weight to hit the same price — the classic race to the bottom</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p class="text-theme-secondary mb-4">
        The mature way to read the cluster: treat every quote as a claim to be verified, not a price to be accepted. The cheapest quote in Anping is almost never the cheapest landed cost in your warehouse — the difference hides in wire diameter, zinc weight, and packaging.
      </p>
